04 / The actual battle engine

Use pure rule resolution plus a separate presentation layer. An attempt has a battle ID, roster/formation and stat snapshots, content version, chosen tactic and reproducible RNG seed. Produce ordered events with actor, intended and actual target, skill, reason, roll, Wound/status source, shield and HP deltas, Chakra and resulting KO. Render animations, timeline and recap from that same event stream. Pause, 1×, 2×, reduced motion and replay must not change the outcome or advance the wallet.

Exactly five deployed units: two front, three rear; any owned role may occupy any slot. Default front K-01 left/K-03 right, rear K-12/K-19/selected support. Freeze initiative at each round start by effective Speed descending; tie by seeded alternating side priority then slot order. One normal action per living unit per round. At slot start process Wound before action selection, check defeat and Stun, then choose legal Ultimate, eligible ready Technique, otherwise Basic. Silence forces a legal Basic. A two-slot Technique cooldown blocks the next TWO own slots: a round-1 cast normally becomes available again at the fourth owner slot. Dead units cannot act. End immediately on the last enemy KO or party wipe. PvE cap is 12 rounds; reaching it without a victory cannot award a first clear.

Target the skill's legal set, resolve eligible Taunt, then one interception, revalidate. Basics respect the selected free tactic then lowest current HP% front, then rear, ties by slot. Frontline First, Focus Mark and Break Threat reorder legal targets only. A row attack can bypass a single-target redirect. No implicit rear access, manual mid-battle skill override or action-bar extra turns.

Personal Chakra starts at 0, clamps to 0–100. Basic +25, Technique +15. A qualifying enemy direct root action gives the defender +5 once when post-mitigation pre-Shield damage is positive, at most +15 per defender per round. A qualifying KO gives +10 once to the root actor. Allied battery gains cap at +15 per recipient per round. At the owner's slot a legal Ultimate spends 100 and gives no ordinary Chakra. A full meter with no legal Ultimate is retained and falls through to legal Technique/Basic. Follow-ups and Wound cannot farm resource triggers. Use explicit action rules when a worked table omits a resource event. For example, the §51.2 shorthand about all three attackers ending at 15 must not erase K-19's qualifying incoming hit and root-action KO. Log that reconciliation in the draft.

Use §24.6 and §27. Start with ATK after the strongest Attack Down (cap 40%). Multiply coefficient, Attack Bonus (cap +40%), Skill/Type Bonus (cap +25%), DEF multiplier, Vulnerability (cap +15%), Crit factor and non-DEF damage reduction (cap 30%). Effective DEF = max(0, DEF × (1 − min(0.40, DEF Down + DEF Penetration))). DEF multiplier = max(0.35,1000/(1000+effectiveDEF)). Floor the resulting hit once, then consume shields (earliest expiry first), then HP. Crit chance cap 75%, Crit damage cap 2×. Direct attacks land; status rolls are independent, applied after damage unless a skill explicitly says otherwise. Ordinary same-name effects follow their refresh rules. Heal up to missing HP with healing bonus capped +25% and suppression capped 40%. Shields share a 40%-of-recipient-Max-HP ceiling.

Wound lasts the target's next two action slots, potentially starting in the same round. Each tick uses 18% of the source's snapshotted ATK after Attack Down and before temporary Attack Bonus. Apply the shared 20%-of-victim-Max-HP raw cap before mitigation, maximum two distinct sources, same-source refresh. For two sources on one target use §49.6’s proportional allocation. Wound can be shielded, persists after source death while combat continues, cannot crit or generate Chakra, and never adds a third tick. For future cards preserve Stun's shared diminishing returns, Silence's Basic fallback, Interrupt canceling only a named charge, round-delayed Speed changes, declared revives, nonrecursive reactions and decoys without full turns or faction counts. See §§24–27 and 47–49.

